# Hei Bai's sacrifice is optional ("you may", CR 608.2d) and the counters only come "if you do" (CR 608.2c). Cast on turn 1 with Black
# Lotus and Mox Pearl, Bot1 declines as it enters (still 3/3, Mox Pearl kept) and again on turn 3 when it attacks with an Ornithopter
# beside it (3 damage, Bot2 17). Bot2 then exiles it with Swords to Plowshares: its "leaves the battlefield" ability puts the (no) counters it had
# on the Ornithopter, its one legal target: the Ornithopter is still 0/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance
Ornithopter
Plains x3
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Swords to Plowshares
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Types = Artifact
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance.Power = 3
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Hei Bai, Spirit of Balance = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Tapped = false
